id: pm-gh1777
title: "GH-1777: pm package list prints the bundled catalog instead of the installed packages, and the four package listings take different --fields contracts"
description: "GH-1777 (filed 2026-11-24 from a project with two npm-installed packages). pm package list, pm packages list and pm extension list are Commander aliases of pm package catalog (alias contract owner pm-ya7x55), so the most natural question an agent asks, which packages does this tracker have, prints the 13 bundled first-party packages (11,976 B toon on this repo) with installed=false rows and none of the packages actually installed. The installed set is spread across explore (5,991 B), manage (6,018 B, each row embeds the full contributions JSON and it is the only listing with update metadata) and inventory (526 B, static, one line per package). catalog accepts --fields; manage, explore and inventory refuse it with unknown_option. pm extensions list (plural) is refused as an unknown command and the did-you-mean suggests package, package activate, package adopt, none of which lists anything. Reproduced on 2026.11.25 in this repo. The report's hub ran seven-week-old extensions because only manage --json exposes update_available. pm-fr6u17 (closed, GH-937) fixed alias rows inside the catalog, not which listing list names. Duplicate check: searched package list installed catalog inventory, extension list did you mean, package manage fields; no open owner."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[5]: agent-ux,extensions,"gh:1777",packages,token-efficiency
created_at: "2026-11-25T05:51:18.663Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-25T08:47:44.772Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-25T07:16:03.640Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-25T07:16:03.640Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "pm package list (and pm packages list, pm extension list) lists the packages installed in the selected scope, and pm package catalog keeps listing the bundled catalog; the alias contract, help, completion and contracts agree; Each package listing (list/inventory, explore, manage, catalog) accepts the same --fields contract and refuses an unknown field with the allowed values; pm package manage rows leave the embedded contributions map out unless requested with --fields, because pm package describe maps them; pm extensions list suggests pm package list"
parent: pm-ugqx
risk: medium
confidence: medium
reporter: unbraind
severity: medium
resolution: "pm package list, pm packages list and pm extension list are now aliases of the static inventory (installed packages in the selected scope, no extension code activated), with an update column from the last pm package manage observation and an updates_available count; pm package catalog keeps the bundled catalog. list, explore, manage and catalog share one --fields contract on the CLI and in the MCP/SDK explore and manage action schemas; an unknown key is refused with the listing's whole domain. Default explore and manage rows leave out the embedded contributions map. pm extensions list now suggests package list with an executable help retry, through a new singular/plural noun step that leaves real commands and aliases to the existing ranking. Alias contracts, grammar rows, flag contracts, help, completion, the static fast path, the dogfood script and the contracts fixture agree."
expected_result: "An agent that runs pm package list sees exactly the installed packages in a few hundred bytes, and every listing answers --fields the same way"
actual_result: "On this repo pm package list prints the 4 installed packages in 574 B (was 11,976 B of catalog); explore and manage rows dropped from about 6.0 KB to 3.8 KB; --fields works on all four listings and refuses unknown keys with the domain; pm extensions list suggests package list"
